Z||000008||Fierowrecker||10-21-2001||08:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Maybe he saw your sig here and thought he'd show you the same respect you show others. (including you attitude towards Police Officers)<BR>Just a thought.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ATTITUDE!!??!! I AIN'T GOT NO F*****G ATTITUDE!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haagster||10-21-2001||08:38 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pepper:<BR><B>I think he was jealous about your car<BR>or his wife had an headache last night so he couldn't f**k her in her ass and that's why he wound do you a favor cops are al the same way ...assholes !!! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You're kidding, right?!?  One cop, on one traffic stop issues a (maybe bogus and sad) citation, and all of the sudden ALL cops are "assholes"?  <P>Whether you like it or not (although we may think he could have used some degree of discretion...) the cop was doing his job.  That's why we hire them.  They are (essentially) our "guard dogs".<P>Grinthock, When you go to court, PLEAD INSANITY!!!  Beg for mercy!!!  Bring the judge an apple...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BTW:  I still think we were ROBBED  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_8.jpg">   <BR>87GT Auto||||reg||1
Z||000010||Haagster||10-21-2001||08:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B> He gives me some story about how the biggest threat in burlington is traffic and that they are focusing on that.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I guess the number of burglary, homicide, drug, rape, etc cases is down to the point where the police are actively concerned with whether or not your headlights are on (after dark, I assume)...  Consider yourself lucky to live in such a safe area...  Apparently the cops are doing their job(s)...<P>In Carlisle, PA (during car show season), the biggest threat to public safety on the streets at 4:30AM is window tint (I'll show you that citation if you're interested). <P><p>[This message has been edited by Haagster (edited 10-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Brian87egotrip||10-21-2001||09:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pepper:<P>cops are al the same way ...assholes !!!<P>NL bryce[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Do you really think all cops assh*les? Yeah, maybe what he did was wrong but would you think he was an ass when he comes to your 911 call becuase someone is breaking into your house or stealing you fiero? How about the NYC cops who gave thier lives to save people?   Just my .02 plus taxes worth<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||hugh||10-21-2001||09:42 AM||||Grinthock got screwed,tough,but that stuff happens.If he showed that cop the same attitude he shows Cliff,he's lucky he didn't get locked up!<BR>Blackstang95,after reading some of the threads you have been involved in,I think it's you who need sympathy!<BR> Pepper,Maybe you should leave the forum,grow up a little then come back.||||reg||13
Z||000013||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-21-2001||10:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B><P><BR>So I walk over to the cop, and no bull ****  I said "Listen, I just lost my job a week ago, I can't even pay next months rent let alone this ticket, can you cut me some slack?"  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I dont know about there, but if someone gets out of their car here and tries to confront a cop about a ticket, they would take it as agression..   <BR>When a cop says to "wait here, I'll be back in a minute" or something,  <P>He/She MEANS it!!  (for their own safety and yours)<P>When he went to your car, how do you know he wasnt going to write up a warning ticket for you, but since he felt agression from you, he decided to give you the ticket and let you share your agression with the judge?<P>Do yourself and the officer a favor next time..<P>1. be straight and to the point (dont ramble or try to lie, they are used to it and know when you do it)<BR>2. have your papers ready<BR>3. dont act suspicious or like you have anything to hide<BR>4. treat them with respect, they have family also and they are putting their life in danger everyday doing their job<BR>5. be polite (works miracles)<BR>6. wait for your turn to talk..dont interupt them or argue (dont agree with it? thats why they can give you a date with a judge to give your side of the story)<P>When I was a teenager, I was a big rebel,and didnt care much for the cops that lived around me, but now that I am married and planning a family, I definely respect the job they do to keep the roads safe for my family.<P>Im sure a few of the officers on this forum would agree with what I wrote here..<P>Who knows? this info might save you a fine next time.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Fformula88||10-21-2001||10:43 AM||||I can certainly understand being upset at the cop for issuing the ticket.  Besides just doing his job, however, he wasn't issuing a bogus citation.  Grinthock even admits he didn't have the lights on.<P>As for there being more dangerous things for cops to watch, don't you think people driving around at night without there lights on isn't dangerous?  There are a reason these things are on a car.  Maybe other drivers would see him with the parking lights... but what if there was another car without lights on or a pedestrain or obstacle in the road?  Without having his own lights on he might have hit the obstacle.  I don't like having the Fiero headlights up either, but I do like to see at night.  Not to avoid tickets but to see well.  Thats just my $.02.... and on that the cop still could have been fogiving.  Just be sure to follow isthis's advise!  Cops do not put up with attitude or BS.||||reg||1
Z||000015||grinthock||10-21-2001||11:33 AM||||I wasn't giving him attitude at all, infact when he came to the car I said how's it goin, I was friendly so was he, the whole time!  I wasn't confrontational, I told him the truth, "Geez honest mistake officer I just left that well lit parking lot" he even said he understood.<P>As for going over to his car, I was already out of my car.  CAuse I asked him if I could get out to get my license, cause it was in my back pocket of my jeans and hard to get to.||||reg||1
Z||000016||FieroLisa||10-21-2001||11:42 AM||||I'm not tryin to stand up for anyone, but whenever someone else complains about a ticket, whatever it may be for, people reply with their sympathy (or cop-bashing).  So why does one person get b*tched at?? Of course cops do their jobs by saving lives and answering 911 calls, but when the rest of you get tickets I'm pretty sure you don't think to yourself "Well dang, I was endangering someone's life, so I guess I deserve this, Thanks so much officer!" <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">     <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000017||Pheagey||10-21-2001||03:18 PM||||Ok, ok my turn for a cop story...<P>   Im heading to college at about 7:50 after stopping by a coffee shop to see a freind. the posted limit on this road is 30. Im comming around one of the curves and trucking alone at 40-45. On this curve a road to the left joins up at such an angle that unless you acually look over you miss the road. So alone Im goin and about 10-15sec. after passing this intersection BAM! sires. So I pit on my flashers, slow down, and pull over (bumpy ride since my shock are shoot). I rool down my window and the cop walkes up.<BR>Cop: whats the hurry?<BR>Me: no hurry hurry office.<BR>Cop: &lt;sternly&gt; Whast the hurry?<BR>ME: Really office no big hurry.<BR>Cop: Do you know how fast you were going?<BR>Me: mmm 30 maybe 35.<BR>Cop: Try closer to 45 son.<BR>me: Ooo, sorry about that office I'll pay closer attention to my speed from now on.<BR>Cop: You do that becuase next time its a ticket.<BR>the cop walk back andnI drive off as he follows mne for a few block;l I get to school w/o event.<BR>   Now the reall big thing about this was this: I had an out of state expires license plate, from kentucky! Down here that jail time if your busted like that. I truly beleive my nicness and honsty keep me out of jail.<BR>   LESSON: be nice, it always pays...<BR>My 2c anyways...||||reg||14
Z||000018||Mach10||10-21-2001||04:18 PM||||One night, cruisng in the Jag, I didn't notice that I had left the lights off. The dash light had popped a little while earlier. Cops pull me over, and the officer walks up. <BR>"Good evening officer, how can I help you?"<BR>"Evening, sir. Are you aware that your headlights are off?"<BR>"Oh bugger... They are? We've been having some electrical problems... I don't have any indicator lamps... (click) There... Sorry about that."<BR>"No problem sir. May I have your license/registration please?"<BR>"Sure thing... Here you go."<BR>"Thank you. This won't take a minute, we'll have you on the way."<BR>"Thanks!"<BR>...<BR>...<BR>"(bottom of stomach drops out) Oh **** ! Did I renew my license?!?"<BR>...<BR>...<BR>"Uh Sir, are you aware that you don't have a valid license? Your license expired 9 days ago."<BR>"Ahhhhhhhhh, CRAP. I was just there 2 weeks ago replacing a stolen license. I think I forgot to renew at the same time..."<BR>"Does your passenger have a license?"<BR>"Yes he does"<BR>"Where do you live?"<BR>"Just at the end of this street."<BR>"Change drivers. Here's your citation."<BR>"*sigh* Thank you officer."<BR>"I'll give you some advice. Go to the magistrate, and explain to him or her how you did to me. Notice that there is no fine on that citation. If you use the same attitude you did with me, it will most likely stay that way. Otherwise, it can go up to a $500 fine. Have a good evening, and don't drive until you renew, ok?"<BR>"Thanks officer!"<P><BR>The cop DIDN'T have to give you the ticket. But you DID leave your lights off. Just show up in court, and show that it was a honest mistake. I got off, there's no reason you shouldn't either. ||||reg||6
Z||000019||BlackStang95||10-21-2001||06:12 PM||||Cops in general really do suck.  Yes those in NYC have worked hard lately, and im sure there are plenty out there, but in all my experiences they are total assholes.  I'll tell you several stories why I feel this way. <P>1. My first encounter ever with a cop.  Me and my friend are parked outside AutoZone (in a legal spot), putting my K+N filter in, and this pig comes up, asks us what we are doing (lol) and then says the alarm at this dinky bait store went off and accuessed us of trying to break in (to steal worms??).  After running my license through he tells us to leave and we do. <P>2.  Three times I was pulled over and told to remove these cool flashing red lights (knight rider style) that I put under the front license plate...this looked really cool so I never wanted to do it but I finally did. <P>3.  Ok, this one was prolly my fualt but ill tell it anyway, this stupid kid walks slowly in front of me as im leaving school, so once he finally moves I light up the back tires a bit.  The cop there freaks out like I just shot someone.  He didn't write a ticket but I got suspended.<P>4.  Three times I have been pulled over and harassed for absolutely nothing.  I mean seriously nothing.  One officer claimed he thought I was vandalizing a school cuz i turned around in its parking lot.  Totally ridiculous, cops are evil people and many of them deserve to be shot.  <P>Flame me if you want, but thats the way it is.||||reg||1
