Z||000023||Fierowrecker||10-21-2001||09:39 PM||||OK, cofession time!<P>Every time I have been pulled over 'cept once or twice, I deserved it...<P>Those times I deserved getting pulled over, did I get a ticket? Once in a while...<P>Why didn't I always get a ticket? I told the truth, and I made it humorus, like the time I was going past 85 in a 55, when the cop asked if I knew how fast I was going, I said "No, my spedo quits at 85, but I guess about 125", He said "Not quite, Sammy..."<BR>He got the joke, and I got off...<P>Those times I got pulled over when I didn't deserve it? The cops wanted to see my engine!!! (That was when I had my Nova with a built 350)<P>Do I resent the cops for doing their jobs? NO! Because most cops get to know the bad apples by the way they drive!<BR>I have called in bad drivers, and usually, I get the comment "Oh ya, we know that jerk..."<P>As for the comments about crime solving, that is usually a different department, with the traffic cops acting as the eyes and ears ON THE STREETS...<P>So all you fine officers of the law, I salute you and the fine job you do!<BR>I know I couldn't handle half the horror you see and deal with every day...<BR>I am surprised you don't have the attitude we are ALL bad!<P>(SUCK UP!!! SUCK UP!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000024||northstarfieroorbust||10-21-2001||10:18 PM||||Well heres my 2cents on the whole thing.  I agree with those that believe that the cops are in general just doing there jobs.  I have had cops unjustly follow me for no reason and have confronted them on it (without getting an attitude with them and without getting cited).  But all the tickets have been justified, ive gotten one accident ticket and one speeding ticket.  The speeding ticke and the accident ticket were both recieved within the first year of my driving.  But because i was polite and respectful to the officers the fines were lower.  And my life was easier for it.  <BR>Give the guys a break, there doing there job and 99 percent of the time are justified.<P>I wasnt happy with my tickets but hey, when your in the wrong your in the wrong.  Let it go and chalk it up to experience. And thats my 2 cents||||reg||1
Z||000025||BlackStang95||10-21-2001||10:40 PM||||Mach10, you are a joke and any future postings by you will be ignored by me.  <P>Cops doing their job?  Is it their job to pull me over for no reason?  I didn't think so.  Explain to me how anything i was doing (see above) was in any way dangerous or wrong (besides the burn out)?  I don't think you can.  <P>People act like cops are in someway better than us.  They're not.  They are average people given a gun and a badge.  I could be one if I wanted.  Isn't that a scary thought?<BR>Any idiot you see could become a cop.  When they're a cop, they're still an idiot, but an idiot with power.  That's dangerous.  Peace.||||reg||1
Z||000026||artherd||10-21-2001||10:51 PM||||You have got to be kidding me...<P>What has become of the fourm these days?!<BR>Honestly, you should all be ashamed of yourselves!<P>Now go to your room, and don't come out untill you've thought about what you've done!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000027||Back On Holiday||10-21-2001||11:17 PM||||I have a couple storys for ya, 1st off...<BR>Needed new tires for inspection, car was past inspection for about 2 months, anyway I approached a 4 way traffic light to make a right turn, 2 lanes each direction.  turn right and in the median is a state cop, I was 19 at the time and I saw him look right at the stickers and since there was traffic behind me, he couldn't pull right out, I saw him pull off the median and try a u-turn into the gas station on the corner and come out as I made a right turn into an industrial park (downhill a bit)  I cruised through there and back out to where I was, but instead of going right I went straight.  and since I was SO close to the PA/DE state line, I just went the back roads till I hit DE and then I got my tires.  &lt;Phew&gt;<BR>Next year, I had problems getting my 84 inspected(the emmisons actually) and it was expired by 3 months, finally got it figured out and inspected.  the SAME day a state cop is sitting in the median watching people in the passing lane of the bypass, thankfully I slowed down in time, but he pulled out behind me and pulled me over.  asked me when I got inspected, told him just this morning. here he tells me that these are the NEW stickers issued after october(my reg is for june) and he saw the 06 and wanted to make sure they were legit.  he looked under the windshield and everything to verify the mileage and such.  he was cool about it.<BR>my 3rd event:  happened 09/24/01, I was on my way to the back doctor and I was just a hair late, I pulled out of my driveway and 15 seconds later a rental type van blows the stop sign on an adjoining road at about 20mph and pulls RIGHT in front of me, he proceeds to go 25-30 in a 35 zone, and is all over the place, I see in his mirror that he is using a Cell-phone and can't concentrate on what he's doing.  I start getting pissed, this goes on for 2 miles until we hit a T intersection, He turns right (the way I want to go) without a turn signal, and WITHOUT stopping (or slowing below 10mph) so *I* slow down and downshift and pull behind and check the opposite lane, CLEAR...so I pass (this is also a 35 zone, but the road is a straight-away) but, like most roads in PA, there is no "dotted" yellow in the middle which states your allowed to pass.<BR>anyway, I was 3/4 passed him when I see a state cop flying behind us and I passed and I see him come around the truck and flash his lights at me, I turn left onto a rural side street and stop.  He gets out and asks me what I was doing, I tell him the truth, the guy in the truck pulled in front of me right past my house and was driving all over the road while using his cellphone.  He Then asked me if I was driving with a suspended license, I told him no, He then said that he believed me about the truck, said that the speed limit was 35 and without radar knew I exceeded it, and that I passed in a no passing zone.  I told him I was sorry, that I knew it was wrong, and I wanted to get away from the crazy guy in the truck.  <BR>He asked for my info, went to his cruiser for a couple mins (guess he ran my info) came back and told me that he was giving me a warning, and that next time go a different way if someone's doing something stupid like that.  I thanked him and proceeded to go THE SPEED LIMIT all the way to the doc appointment(I made it on time too!)<BR>Moral: Tell the truth, most of the time they KNOW your lying! <P>ps, the suspended license thing?  I think he thought I may be that idiot that works at radio shack down the road who's got a Blue 87GT and a 88 red re-bodied car who lost his license for 4 years for driving w/o a license and for speeding etc..  I tried getting that blue GT, but he backed out of the deal. (he didn't show up and when I called, said....I can't find the title, uhhh my mom won't let me sell it, uhhh the cars not here, my friends got it)<BR>finally he admitted he didn't want to sell it til the fall.  well, forget it now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Back On Holiday (edited 10-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000028||Oreif||10-22-2001||02:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B> They are average people given a gun and a badge.  I could be one if I wanted.  Isn't that a scary thought?<BR>Any idiot you see could become a cop.  When they're a cop, they're still an idiot, but an idiot with power.  That's dangerous.  Peace.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>See you just said it yourself. They are average people. Most average young teenagers like yourself, do many stupid things. Since the Police Officers were once teenagers and most likely did the same stupid things, They are good at recognizing idiots doing stupid things. So trying to lie your way out of a ticket isn't going to work. Also, since they are average people, they know when someone gives them "attitude" they are usually idiots who have done something wrong. I am not saying all Officers are good, I have been stopped by a few who were on a "Power Trip" but the thing that drives these ego-manics crazy is to be polite, honest, and smile alot.<BR>With working night shift I usually get stopped an average of 4 times a year. Mostly they are looking for drunk drivers. Occasionally (maybe once a year) I'll get a ticket for speeding. (which I happen to do once in a while  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  ) Yes, I have been stopped for some pretty lame excuses like 41 in a 40 zone, (No ticket)<BR>But I don't mind. They are doing their job just like I do mine. In fact usually after being stopped, The Officer will recognize me and know I'm on my way home from work. So if he sees me driving a little "fast" he may just let it slide or he'll pull next to me at a light and ask me to slow it down a bit. Finally with them stopping and looking for drunk drivers (and crazed teenage idiots) It is a whole lot safer for me to drive home. I don't have to worry as much about getting killed by some drunk fool or some inexperienced teenages racing around. <P><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Haagster||10-22-2001||02:12 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>You have got to be kidding me...<P>What has become of the fourm these days?!<BR>Honestly, you should all be ashamed of yourselves!<P>Now go to your room, and don't come out untill you've thought about what you've done!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ditto.<P>I'm sorry I chimed in on this one.  This thread is getting way off topic.  What say we all grow up a little and stop the cop bashing...<p>[This message has been edited by Haagster (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000030||Sleeper||10-22-2001||02:32 AM||||hey, Grinthock. it sounds like your city is desperately in need of money. they do the same sh*t here, instead of raising the taxes they start giving out B.S. tickets like yours or too bright of lights, broken head/tail light, windsheid banners, a mile or 2 over the speed limit, etc, etc. anything to get them some money.||||reg||1
Z||000031||Mach10||10-22-2001||03:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Mach10, you are a joke and any future postings by you will be ignored by me.  <P>Cops doing their job?  Is it their job to pull me over for no reason?  I didn't think so.  Explain to me how anything i was doing (see above) was in any way dangerous or wrong (besides the burn out)?  I don't think you can.  <P>People act like cops are in someway better than us.  They're not.  They are average people given a gun and a badge.  I could be one if I wanted.  Isn't that a scary thought?<BR>Any idiot you see could become a cop.  When they're a cop, they're still an idiot, but an idiot with power.  That's dangerous.  Peace.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Oh-ho-ho-ho... I'm a joke huh? You've cut me to the quick... I truly feel sorry for the people who have to hang around you all day. All those bad vibes 'n stuff.<P>1) YES it is their job to pull you over. I have no idea what you look like, but considering that you fall easily into the category of higher statistical probability of committing a crime, of course you are going to get pulled over. Funny that. Neither me nor my friends EVER get pulled over for stuff we didn't do. Ever consider that the guy with the gun DOESN'T have the extra chromasomes in the situation? Funny how it's the guy in charge who's always at fault. Do you have a thing against authority?<P>1) Hmm... In a parking lot, near where a silent alarm has been triggered. Who the hell do you THINK they're gonna go after? Who's the only people around doing WEIRD things? Installing car parts in a parking lot is pretty odd... I think they were perfectly justified. Did you get a ticket? No? Then shut up.<BR>2) Didn't you know? They're illegal. You can't have flashing red, white, or blue lamps on a non-emergency vehicle, (excepting red and yellow factory turn-signals), so that you aren't distracting/confusing/annoying other drivers.<BR>3) No comment. None needed.<BR>4) Just cause. It's called keeping the peace. Route out any suspicious behavior, and investigate. Again, did you get a ticket?<P>I truly hope that one day, when your home has been invaded, and you're trying to dial 9-1-1, but your wife's blood is making the buttons too slippery, that the police officer that shows up never hears what your stupid fool mouth (fingers) has said here. You know, he might just decide to pull over that speeder instead.<P><BR>Oh-oh-oh... Maybe *YOU* have a better idea as to how to keep the streets safe? Any idiot with a gun, huh? Do you have ANY idea what has to happen before you are accepted into the academy? <BR>Are you an Anarchist? Do you believe in self-government? Maybe you were assaulted as a child by a teddy-bear in a police uniform. I can't think of any other reason for this rank excrement streaming from your mouth (fingers)... <P>Grow up. And while you're at it, do the rest of us a favor and fnck off. Unless, of course, you have something relevant and/or intelligent to say?||||reg||3
Z||000032||fierohoho||10-22-2001||06:32 AM||||I come to this forum to relax and forget about work and keep company with other people who like Fieros and have to put up with people who apparently have their lives  totally ruined to the point where it seems they can no longer function and feel good unless they put down a profession they know absolutly nothing about.<P>You got a ticket? Boo F'in Hoo.<P>Take a little responsibility for your own actions and grow up, it's called being an adult.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif">   <P>[This message has been edited by fierohoho (edited 10-22-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by fierohoho (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000033||BlackStang95||10-22-2001||10:31 AM||||Wow you really blew a head gasket mach.  I'm truly sorry if I pushed you over the edge and you are now insane.  To wish what you said on someone you sincerely have to be a far worse individual than me, I wouldn't wish that on anyone, even your sorry ass.  As for homes being invaded, it would take the cops 5-10 minutes to arrive, they'd be way too late.  I'm sure I would handle anyone with my .45 or MAC-10.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  For you if you were here and said that to my face I think id use the classic brass knuckles or maybe a nice butterfly knife.  Too bad you're so far away and talking ****  like a ***** .  Your preoccupation with molestation and homosexuality makes it easy to see you are gay. Take a chill pill up your gay ass man, and relax.  It's just a damn thread.  Lol.  <P>also about the red lights, I know they are illegal, but it bugs me to see me getting harassed for one little thing when i see ricers all the time looking like ufo's riding around with impunity.<P>In general I like the police, they are no doubt needed, but there are far too many, at least in my town, on ego trips that have nothing better to do than to harass me and other innocent law abiding citizens.<BR>Just to clear things up, I don't have any tickets, points or otherwise, sparkling clean driving record, how you like dem apples?  I'm just tired of being harassed. <P>The rest of what I see on this thread is nothing but old-fashioned young people bashing and stereotypes.  Oh no, no one young could ever drive well, or better than you, or know more about cars than you.  There's something in the Bible against that.  Get over yourselves.  ||||reg||1
